APPENDIX I. Petitions Voted on by FWHFFL owners between 2011 & 2022:

1) Remove the Kicker roster spot. FAIL (5-6)

1.1) Change scoring system for kickers to: All FG=3, PAT=1, MISS= -2 PASS (10-1)

2) Add a Coach Roster spot. FAIL (3-8)

3) Allow for unlimited keepers, but keep the same dollar rules for keepers ($10 more for first year, etc.)

PASS (6-5)

4) Add 1/2 or 1 point per reception to the scoring. FAIL (2-9)

5) Add an IR roster spot. PASS (8-3)

6) Add 1 points per 50 return yards to special teams / players. FAIL (3-8)

7) Allow for TE to be used in the FLEX spot. PASS (11-0)

8) Change the waiver system to a silent bidding system. (Ex. you start with $100 and can bid on waivers

throughout the season. If you win a player, that money is subtracted from your $100) PASS (9-2)

9) Change scoring to decimals (1 rushing yard is .1 points) PASS (8-2-1)

10) Leftover money after the auction draft added to the silent bidding system, or carries over to the draft

next season. FAIL (5-6)

11) Change from 2 conferences to 4 divisions. FAIL (1-9-1)10

12) Wild Card playoff teams are based on points for and not record. (You can vote for either 5th and 6th

seed, 6th seed only, or none) PASS (8-3) - 6th seed only.

13) Contract buyout options for dropping players signed for a 2 year keeper contract. Heist proposes a

cap hit of 75% of the keeper value if you drop the player. EX. Fosters 2nd year would be $41 dollars, so if

Heist dropped him, he would take a cap hit of $31 and lose Foster for the final year. The cap hit

percentage is also up for vote. FAIL (3-8)

14) Commish cannot make waiver claims. He can only set lineups, push/kill trades and make free agent

pick ups for other teams. PASS (10-1)

15) Rosters locking for playoffs should also come with a roster expansion emulating the September

roster expansion of Major League Baseball. FAIL (1-9-1)

16) The vetoing system needs to be reworked. We can either leave it the same, change it to Commish

reviews trades only, or have a trade review committee of a few people who review each trade to decide

if they are fair. TBD

16.1) Votes for passing or vetoing a trade must be posted to the league message board or

relayed to the commissioner. 6 votes needed to veto a trade. PASS (unanimous)

17) The name of the trophy: Alex Teves Memorial Cup. PASS (unanimous)

18) Trade inception rule to replace the Trade veto process. PASS (unanimous)

1. A 24 hour clock starts from the time of an accepted trade whereby competing offers may

be submitted for 1 of the players involved in the trade.

2. If a trade is intercepted the 24 hour clock starts over. In the event of a further

interception the player from the original deal has to be included in the new deal.

19) Allow league dues to be paid via Google Wallet or Venmo. PASS (unanimous)

20) Remove 2 division system in favor of 1 division. PASS (unanimous)

20.1) Institute “rivalry” scheduling. PASS (unanimous)

21) Allow off-season keeper trades. PASS (7-5)

22) 3 Way Trades. FAIL (3-8)

23) Remove D/ST. FAIL (2-9)11

